@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `nii-il05-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il05-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-k`
IMPORT `nii-s348-maximum-minimum`
IMPORT `nii-s342-liability-and-deduction`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-05: National Insurance Law Schedule K, ss 342, 348.
--
-- Imports this row's nouns and refusals and IL-05's modules, and no other row.
-- Exposes numbers. IL-05 declares its own copies of IL-04's `A branch of
-- insurance` and `A column of insured persons in Schedule J` (RECONCILE.md,
-- clash N1); here the constructors are IL-05's. The column D amounts arrive in
-- this row's record from the IL-04 adapter and are matched to IL-05's branches
-- by name.
--
-- THE EARNER AS IL-05 SEES IT (input conventions, BRIEF.md "The household"):
-- an employee (s 1, row IL-04) for a month; income from work the monthly
-- salary, no income not from work; contributions payable in every branch s 335
-- imposes on an employee (s 335 is not encoded; IL-04's tests read all nine
-- branches for an employee, and the Institute's composites confirm them, IL-04
-- NOTES.md section 5); no unemployment benefit, no s 348(e) status, s 350(c)
-- not reached, no order under s 348(c); no senior citizen pension; not a police
-- or prison officer; no regulations under s 342(e)(3)-(4) govern the deduction.
--
-- VERSION 0.2.0 SUPERSEDES two of these: the branches are s 335's answer (row
-- IL-08), passed in this row's record `IL-07 branches in which contributions
-- are payable for the earner`; and a woman's age under Schedule A1 Part D is the
-- age row IL-08 computes from her date of birth, passed in, not read from the
-- earner record. The 0.1.0 rules that read them are replaced below.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-05`

§§ `Section 348 — the income on which contributions are computed`

GIVEN e IS AN `IL-07 earner`
GIVETH A MAYBE `The minimum wage applicable to the employee in the first month of each quarter`
`IL-05: the minimum wage applicable to the earner` e MEANS
    IF   e's `the full monthly minimum wage of an employee aged 18 or over applies to the earner`
    THEN JUST `the full monthly minimum wage in the first month of each quarter of 2026`
    ELSE `IL-07 holds Schedule K's minimum only for an employee to whom the full monthly minimum wage of an adult applies`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
`IL-05: the earner's month under section 348, in` h MEANS
    `An insured person's period under section 348` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS h's `the year of the month`
        `period`                                                              IS `a month of the tax year` (h's `the month of the year`)
        `column`                                                              IS `an employee`
        `income from work in the period`                                      IS h's `the earner`'s `the earner's monthly salary`
        `income not from work in the period, not exempt under section 350`    IS 0
        `the minimum wage applicable to the employee`                         IS `IL-05: the minimum wage applicable to the earner` (h's `the earner`)
        `received unemployment benefit for a full month under Chapter G`      IS FALSE
        `a volunteer in national service or in community volunteering`        IS FALSE
        `a student in a Torah institution or in a yeshiva`                    IS FALSE
        `serving in civil service as defined in section 6(a) of the Deferral of Service for Yeshiva Students Law` IS FALSE
        `the day the person began national-civic service, if serving in it`   IS NOTHING
        `section 350(c) disapplies section 348(b) to the person`              IS FALSE
        `an order under section 348(c) has changed a minimum amount for the period` IS FALSE

@ref NII s 348 and Schedule K (row IL-05, nii-s348-maximum-minimum.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-05: the income on which the earner's contributions are computed, in` h MEANS
    `s 348 — the income on which contributions are computed, for` (`IL-05: the earner's month under section 348, in` h)

§§ `Section 342(c) — what the employer deducts from the wage`

GIVEN e               IS AN `IL-07 earner`
      `the Part D age` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The insured person, for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)`
`IL-05: the earner for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)` e `, at a Part D age of` `the Part D age` MEANS
    IF   e's `the earner is a woman`
    THEN CONSIDER `the Part D age`
         WHEN JUST `the months` THEN `a woman` `the months`
         WHEN NOTHING           THEN `the earner is a woman, and the age Part D of Schedule A1 fixes for her is not given`
    ELSE `a man`

-- s 335's answer, in this row's record, as IL-05's list (in Schedule J's order).
GIVEN br IS AN `IL-07 branches in which contributions are payable for the earner`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch of insurance`
`IL-05: the branches, by IL-05's branches` br MEANS
    filter `payable`
        (LIST `maternity`, `children`, `work injury`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`
            , `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`, `disability`, `long-term care`
            , `senior citizens and survivors`)
    WHERE
        `payable` b MEANS
            CONSIDER b
            WHEN `maternity`                                   THEN br's `contributions are payable for maternity`
            WHEN `children`                                    THEN br's `contributions are payable for children`
            WHEN `work injury`                                 THEN br's `contributions are payable for work injury`
            WHEN `accident injury`                             THEN br's `contributions are payable for accident injury`
            WHEN `unemployment`                                THEN br's `contributions are payable for unemployment`
            WHEN `employees' rights in insolvency proceedings` THEN br's `contributions are payable for employees' rights in insolvency proceedings`
            WHEN `disability`                                  THEN br's `contributions are payable for disability`
            WHEN `long-term care`                              THEN br's `contributions are payable for long-term care`
            WHEN `senior citizens and survivors`               THEN br's `contributions are payable for senior citizens and survivors`

GIVEN d IS AN `IL-07 column D amounts on the earner's wage`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A branch's column D amount`
`IL-05: the column D amounts, by IL-05's branches` d MEANS
    LIST `for` `maternity`                     (d's `the column D amount for maternity`)
       , `for` `accident injury`               (d's `the column D amount for accident injury`)
       , `for` `unemployment`                  (d's `the column D amount for unemployment`)
       , `for` `disability`                    (d's `the column D amount for disability`)
       , `for` `long-term care`                (d's `the column D amount for long-term care`)
       , `for` `senior citizens and survivors` (d's `the column D amount for senior citizens and survivors`)
    WHERE
        `for` b x MEANS `A branch's column D amount` WITH `branch` IS b, `amount` IS x

GIVEN h                IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      d                IS AN `IL-07 column D amounts on the earner's wage`
      br               IS AN `IL-07 branches in which contributions are payable for the earner`
      `the Part D age` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An employee's month under section 342(c)`
`IL-05: the earner's month under section 342(c), in` h `, with column D amounts` d `, in the branches` br `, at a Part D age of` `the Part D age` MEANS
    `An employee's month under section 342(c)` WITH
        `tax year`                                                            IS h's `the year of the month`
        `month`                                                               IS h's `the month of the year`
        `branches for which contributions are payable under section 335`      IS `IL-05: the branches, by IL-05's branches` br
        `the column D amounts on the wage`                                    IS `IL-05: the column D amounts, by IL-05's branches` d
        `senior citizen pension`                                              IS `not payable for any of the month`
        `the insured person`                                                  IS `IL-05: the earner for the age limb of section 342(c)(2)` (h's `the earner`) `, at a Part D age of` `the Part D age`
        `date of birth`                                                       IS h's `the earner`'s `the earner's date of birth`
        `a police officer or a prison officer`                                IS FALSE
        `the employer deducts under regulations made under section 342(e)(3) or an approval under section 342(e)(4)` IS FALSE

-- Version 0.2.1: IL-05 v0.3.0 (backlog row IL-11) reads s 342(c)(1)'s "as in Schedule J" at a
-- reading of row IL-04's fork F4 (the printed totals by default). At the items it sums the per-branch
-- amounts in `d`; at the printed totals it takes column D for the deduction branches together, the
-- number the IL-04 adapter computes (`IL-04: column D in a month of …, reading …`).
GIVEN r IS AN `IL-07 a reading of Schedule J column D above the reduced collection threshold`
GIVETH A `A reading of Schedule J where its totals row and its items differ`
`IL-05: the reading` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the printed total of column D`                      THEN `the printed totals govern`
    WHEN `the sum of the items of the six deduction branches` THEN `the items govern`

@ref NII s 342(c) (row IL-05, nii-s342-liability-and-deduction.l4); Schedule J (row IL-04, fork F4)
GIVEN h                IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      d                IS AN `IL-07 column D amounts on the earner's wage`
      br               IS AN `IL-07 branches in which contributions are payable for the earner`
      `the Part D age` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      r                IS AN `IL-07 a reading of Schedule J column D above the reduced collection threshold`
      `at the totals`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-05: the amount the employer deducts from the earner's wage, in` h `, with column D amounts` d `, in the branches` br `, at a Part D age of` `the Part D age` `, reading` r `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals` MEANS
    `s 342(c) — the amount the employer deducts from the wage, for` (`IL-05: the earner's month under section 342(c), in` h `, with column D amounts` d `, in the branches` br `, at a Part D age of` `the Part D age`)
        `, reading Schedule J as` (`IL-05: the reading` r) `, column D at the printed totals being` `at the totals`

-- (Version 0.2.0's `IL-05: the employer deducts in every branch section 342(c)(1)
-- names, …`, which the capstone's own composition of the printed totals read, is
-- removed in 0.2.1: row IL-04 now decides that, NOTES.md section 11.14.)

§§ `Figures IL-05 sourced from the National Insurance Institute (not law)`

@ref National Insurance Institute, 2026 figures (row IL-05, nii-il05-published-figures.l4)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-05: the reduced collection threshold for 2026, as published` MEANS
    `the reduced collection threshold for 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute`

@ref NII Schedule K item 1 (row IL-05, nii-schedule-k.l4), with the 2026 figures
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-05: the Schedule K item 1 maximum for a month of 2026` MEANS
    `Schedule K item 1 — the maximum income for a month, under` `the figures Schedule K reads for 2026, as published`
